  "scientific_review": [
    "The25 frozen previous projection objects remain exactly equal and all prior CSV cells remain unchanged. Four dated model reference scenarios are added: EAC2022-01-15/07-15 at primary5cm/s and Kuroshio2024-01-15/07-15 at primary10cm/s. Current-owned canonical depth IDs refresh from the701-reference v48 register. No new source measurements are created.",
    "All24 original reference nodes remain in source order. Twelve meet their declared lower-depth projection gates. Only four of20original adjacent intervals support conditional interpolation;16remain gaps. Unsupported exact anchors and both neighboring intervals remain unknown. A remote eligible pair is never joined over a blocked intermediate node, and no extrapolation occurs.",
    "EAC retains the frozen join gate: interior model maximum, resolved primary5cm/s lower contour and positive retained second-product surface component. Its only conditional interval in each2022snapshot is original27–30S corridor vertices4–5. Frozen editorial reference distances and positions remain separate from actual selected model-node coordinates. Mooring data remain regional context and do not fill or substitute depths.",
    "Kuroshio retains all five original18.5/21.5/24.5/27.5/29.5N reference gates per2024snapshot. Outer-window maxima at18.5N both dates and24.5N January remain blocked;July24.5N primary10cm/s lower boundary remains censored. Only27.5–29.5N is conditionally joined in eachsnapshot. WGS84 shortest gate connectors are explicit reference geometry, not observed current-axis paths or measured current lengths.",
    "At eligible source nodes retain exact model upper/lower depths and layer span, native connected-layer statuses/brackets, selected model coordinates, locked component bearings and source profile pointers. Lower depth may be projected without a layer span if its upper boundary is unknown. Paired model upper depth/layer span are interpolated only with supported paired endpoints; span remains the difference between threshold boundaries, not physical whole-current thickness.",
    "EAC source snapshots, mapped multi-day surface support and mooring operators remain different. Kuroshio daily GLORYS-derived axis geometry and HYCOM00Z instantaneous velocity are not simultaneous or statistically independent observations. Current identities, dates, primary thresholds and source component frames are kept per case; no pooled seasonal range, common boundary definition or annual extrema is asserted.",
    "Each sample links the exact source anchor(s) it uses. Source model-profile JSON pointers resolve to the selected retained native profiles; reference positions are explicit and distinct. Samples every50km plus each exact source anchor show assumed linear descriptors only where the gate allows. Derived coordinates/values round to six serialization decimals and displayed depth to10m; those digits do not imply physical accuracy or depth confidence intervals.",
    "Fourteen cloud tests verify exact previous25-object/CSV preservation and ownership counts; per-case dates/thresholds/frames; frozen EAC gates and selected model pointers; Kuroshio original edge/censored gates; three-quantity midpoint interpolation; missing-upper semantics; exact/neighbor gap blocking; no extrapolation; invalid distances/order/duplicates/thickness mismatch; source-key mutations; physical eligibility; CSV quantities and pinned inputs. Six baseline tests passed at the same source commit.",
    "The v48 forward clarification is carried visibly at register level: the Spray half-core diagnostic uses a qualifying sampled10–200m core maximum, while its descending search can extend deeper. The previous review phrase full-profile core was imprecise. Old25 objects and source values remain frozen rather than silently rewritten.",
    "All geometry, interpolation and tests ran in cloud on one idle CPU using retained byte-pinned sources; there was no new field retrieval. Local work prepared metadata/code, checked proof hashes and retained exact cloud JSON/CSV bytes. Existing102 eddy-size references and canonical701 scoped depth references remain unchanged.",
    "The inventory now has29regional scenarios across13identities, with98identities still lacking a regional projection scenario. No whole-route physical depth profile, physical current thickness, matched width join, cross-sectional area, volume, state passage, annual envelope or UI/runtime integration is established. The depth programme remains incomplete."
  ],
